 "name": "Insectoid Armor",
 "type": "spell",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/construction.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Construction — Innate Technique (11th level)</em></p><p>At 11th level, you realize you need a way to efficiently use your cursed energy despite being an inefficient technique. You have learned how to create armor that simulates the efficiency of an insect's bug body. As a bonus action for 10 cursed energy, you can surround yourself in this armor and gain the following benefits for 1 hour:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Your Strength, Dexterity, and Armor Class scores increase by +4, as a result of the efficiency of the constructs.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You will gain resistance to non-magical bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage. This becomes immunity at 18th level.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Wings will sprout from your back, granting you a flying speed equal to your walking speed. In addition, you can now use a free action to dash on your turn.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Your unarmed strikes deal two additional damage dice and your unarmed strikes roll one additional damage dice on a critical.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
   "chat": ""
  },
